#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054342 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3de9e532-559c-5fc1-a6ad-5fcd1ed77824" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/id #uuid "e557c534-7392-5c31-9e08-43347736716e" :question/math-academy-id "e-13138" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\n\\mathbb N, \\quad \\mathbb Z, \\quad \\mathbb Q, \\quad \\mathbb R, \\quad \\mathbb C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $3.25$ belong?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $\\mathbb{N}$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $\\mathbb{Z}$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $\\mathbb{Q}$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $\\mathbb{R}$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $\\mathbb C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**.\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following: \n\n- The number $3.25$ is not an integer, so it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Z}$ nor $\\mathbb{N},$  so we can write\n\n$$\n3.25\\notin\\mathbb N, \\qquad 3.25\\notin\\mathbb Z.\n$$\n\n- However, notice that $3.25$ can be written as the ratio of two integers as follows:\n\n$$\n3.25=\\dfrac{325}{100}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $3.25$ is a rational number, and we can write\n\n$$\n3.25 \\in \\mathbb{Q}.\n$$\n\n- Every rational is a real and complex number. Consequently, $3.25$ belongs to both $\\mathbb R$ and $\\mathbb{C},$ and we can write\n\n$$\n3.25 \\in \\mathbb{R}, \\qquad 3.25 \\in \\mathbb{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbb Q, \\mathbb R,$ and $\\mathbb C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054343 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abc6b3ee-0251-5c9c-9358-bd192c434dd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to Scripted Special Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "ce8a56c1-709e-50e8-ac10-d3f92bf15db0" :question/math-academy-id "e-13139" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^-?$\n\n- $-\\sqrt{3}$\n\n- $- 0.2$\n\n- $0$\n\n- $-\\sqrt{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^-$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{3}$ is negative but not a rational number, so it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^-. \\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- $-0.2$ is negative, and it is a rational number because it can be written as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n-0.2 = -\\dfrac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-0.2$ belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^-. \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $0$ is a rational number but not negative, so it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^-. \\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- $-\\sqrt{4} =- 2$, and it is a rational number because it can be written as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt 4 = -2 = -\\dfrac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-\\sqrt 4$ belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^-. \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054344 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/id #uuid "e8b7d098-3cda-548e-b1d3-e1f2a87b59b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-13140" :question/problem "To which of the following sets do all the negative integers belong? \n\n- $\\mathbb{Z}$\n\n- $\\mathbb{Z}_0^+$\n\n- $\\mathbb{Q}^-$\n\n- $\\mathbb{R}_0^-$" :question/worked-solution "The negative integers are $-1, -2, -3, \\ldots$\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains all the integers, including the negative integers. $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}_0^+$ contains the positive integers and $0.$ So, it does not contain the negative integers. $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^-$ contains all the negative rational numbers. Since all integers are rational numbers, $\\mathbb{Q}^-$ contains all the negative integers as well. $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^-$ contains all the negative real numbers and $0.$ Since all integers are real numbers, $\\mathbb{R}_0^-$ contains all the negative integers as well. $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abc6b3ee-0251-5c9c-9358-bd192c434dd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to Scripted Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "def6a70d-48be-5761-80f6-ba7b752831b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301008} {:answer/id #uuid "4d69d869-e49d-5686-b3a3-4d06825320e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301009} {:answer/id #uuid "21fd1b83-20db-52b3-b526-75c6c68639c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301010} {:answer/id #uuid "7b0a4e1d-31c4-5ade-b897-a75dff5173c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301011} {:answer/id #uuid "4179cb41-a737-571d-b6eb-5a1bba0d23a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b0a4e1d-31c4-5ade-b897-a75dff5173c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301011} :answer-field/id #uuid "009034eb-4dfc-5afb-9f77-266c35d15fd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "161da8d4-ccfa-570a-837c-943ddb8b2d13" :question/math-academy-id "q-104694" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to ${Q}^{-}?$\n\n- $47$\n- $-\\sqrt{12}$\n- $\\sqrt{10}$\n- $0$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $47$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\sqrt{12}=-2\\sqrt{3}$ is not a rational number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $\\sqrt{10}$ is positive, not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $0$ is not negative, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None of those listed\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abc6b3ee-0251-5c9c-9358-bd192c434dd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to Scripted Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e67c485-5182-5506-ad5e-768fafd7b998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301015} {:answer/id #uuid "c020362c-8ee6-5e52-9f74-b41e652e39c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301016} {:answer/id #uuid "a732d9aa-e7b1-5375-a39e-ff3980b6e580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301017} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1b0312-524d-5198-b1d1-48e94336a025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301018} {:answer/id #uuid "6a511f2b-2d2a-5aaa-9fc0-0d314913fcc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a732d9aa-e7b1-5375-a39e-ff3980b6e580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301017} :answer-field/id #uuid "f20f165c-4f16-5ab3-afb4-ba1eca836ae1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c8731da-fe89-5dc0-9d91-bfc024644fdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-104702" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${Z}_{0}^{-}?$\n\n- $-62$\n- $0$\n- $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n- $-\\frac{56}{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${Z}_{0}^{-}$ is the set of all negative integer numbers and $0.$\n\n- $-62$ belongs to ${Z}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $0$ belongs to ${Z}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\n- $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is not an integer, so it does *not* belong to ${Z}_{0}^{-}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\frac{56}{4}=-14$ belongs to ${Z}_{0}^{-}.\\,✓$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I, II, and IV only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b5d0ea0-51f2-55cf-a747-05036a7c9ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301022} {:answer/id #uuid "9b87b1c0-8cc1-5596-b8b7-8339ee5181b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301023} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8229f4-e06e-544a-87ae-5ed6fbf8498a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301024} {:answer/id #uuid "f43fe9d7-3077-5876-ad1b-7750f4ad5f4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301025} {:answer/id #uuid "fb3619ca-e8d4-5913-b9a5-9d8c79180de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b5d0ea0-51f2-55cf-a747-05036a7c9ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301022} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5be12c-6c96-5ace-a283-c9005ede7507" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4296d9e0-dc9b-5497-bd2a-d3f329be66fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-104703" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $\\sqrt{121}$ belong?\n\n- $N$\n- ${Q}^{-}$\n- ${Z}^{-}$\n- $Z$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that $\\sqrt{121}=11$ is a natural number, so it belongs to $N.$\n\nSince every natural number is also an integer number, $\\sqrt{121}$ also belongs to $Z.$ \n\nOn the other hand, the sets ${Z}^{-}$ and ${Q}^{-}$ only contain negative numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{121}$ does not belong to either of these sets. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3de9e532-559c-5fc1-a6ad-5fcd1ed77824" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f9235de-2197-5ae9-bd27-c0d6a14174c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301028} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c9bf12-b239-5054-97da-4d2b72922407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301029} {:answer/id #uuid "a2edc4de-f475-51c6-a33c-52ef8777e773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301030} {:answer/id #uuid "5e96ae23-b394-57a8-89f1-d49d944c0d79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N,Z,$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301031} {:answer/id #uuid "40e64332-dea5-52e6-847a-49caff9ff04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40e64332-dea5-52e6-847a-49caff9ff04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301032} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b88e998-8ffc-5d6d-86a5-a629f18e496a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d88d3c9d-ec93-5bf2-a49b-0b326607c0ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-181441" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $\\sqrt{-1}$ belong?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- First, we note that $\\sqrt{-1}=\\text{i}$ is a complex number. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-1}\\in C.\n$$\n\n- Since the imaginary part of $\\sqrt{-1}$ is nonzero, it does not belong to $N,Z,Q,$ or $R.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-1}\\notin N,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin Z,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin Q,\\,\\sqrt{-1}\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3de9e532-559c-5fc1-a6ad-5fcd1ed77824" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f25ca92-8214-57c6-b53f-1b185bd1705b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N,Z,Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301035} {:answer/id #uuid "31416064-8add-5531-9eb6-e4a192b706e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301036} {:answer/id #uuid "9388e54c-899b-543f-9481-9f310341890d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301037} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f0f9b5-21ee-53b5-acdf-50ec5aed16ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301038} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4195a6-44c1-5fef-bbd0-46c52a39fe98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb4195a6-44c1-5fef-bbd0-46c52a39fe98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301039} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c690567-4cf0-5647-bd41-63550a2c951f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac7a530d-d333-5d45-b920-2143ec7f7b31" :question/math-academy-id "q-181522" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $\\sqrt{-4}$ belong?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- First, we note that $\\sqrt{-4}=2\\text{i}$ is a complex number. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-4}\\in C.\n$$\n\n- Since the imaginary part of $\\sqrt{-4}$ is nonzero, it does *not* belong to $N,Z,Q,$ or $R.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-4}\\notin N,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin Z,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin Q,\\,\\sqrt{-4}\\notin R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301040 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0e799c7-61bc-505b-9a77-cb51ab3a241d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301042} {:answer/id #uuid "f59a58e2-6060-507c-aecc-d54c5b4c2c0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301043} {:answer/id #uuid "b470d98c-cd79-5bcf-86fd-f8da7982318b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301044} {:answer/id #uuid "c87efe5f-d8fe-50d8-ac00-ea04c46ca7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301045} {:answer/id #uuid "2c1d0301-f81c-574a-994b-6152fd9ce767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b470d98c-cd79-5bcf-86fd-f8da7982318b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301044} :answer-field/id #uuid "a17abd26-d972-536f-8201-f19d5ec1b77e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f0ed03a-d67b-5694-a70d-e3b447bf54f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-181544" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $-\\pi $ belong?\n\n- ${Q}^{-}$\n- $R$\n- $Q$\n- $C$" :question/worked-solution "The number $-\\pi $ is not a rational number. Consequently, $-\\pi $ does not belong to any of the sets  ${Q}^{-}$ nor $Q.$\n\nHowever, $-\\pi $ is a real number, so it belongs to $R.$\n\nFinally, since every real number is also a complex number, $-\\pi $ also belongs to $C.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b56d6243-84ee-57e2-8b16-8d04ab866104" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301049} {:answer/id #uuid "f6733024-337e-5719-9694-d231e3b90638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301050} {:answer/id #uuid "5533f150-edb5-54ef-be2a-68d0ce1dab32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301051} {:answer/id #uuid "62975e55-d1dc-5003-bb98-f33ec2ca519b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301052} {:answer/id #uuid "dbe0e664-8cd1-59e8-b2f9-6329bf92a0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbe0e664-8cd1-59e8-b2f9-6329bf92a0dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301053} :answer-field/id #uuid "22705392-7660-50ea-bd69-7b644e1f9221" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da5ecc99-4be2-51b4-9f3a-3271207792b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-181545" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $\\frac{1}{\\pi }$ belong?\n\n- $Z$\n- ${Q}^{+}$\n- $Q$\n- $R$" :question/worked-solution "The number $\\frac{1}{\\pi }$ is not an integer nor a rational number. Consequently, $\\frac{1}{\\pi }$ does not belong to any of the sets $Z,$ ${Q}^{+},$ nor $Q.$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{1}{\\pi }$ is a real number, so it belongs to $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28fab9a7-ebda-596c-91da-c7207e77cd9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301056} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d1aed1-ac81-59d9-85b4-ea8833532df5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301057} {:answer/id #uuid "300f0d2c-52b4-5c43-a3e9-ae1f5fcf9cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301058} {:answer/id #uuid "0a5b4981-5eb4-5038-b00b-d136c38be7d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301059} {:answer/id #uuid "1cfdab88-4108-5b8f-942f-53564f0a9d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cfdab88-4108-5b8f-942f-53564f0a9d97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301060} :answer-field/id #uuid "9160b50a-9e2c-581c-80fc-99ce30c0d328" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73e9e1c2-5834-596e-8e52-184fa8e24c9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36248" :question/problem "To which of the following sets do all the positive integers belong?\n\n- $N$\n- ${R}^{+}$\n- ${Q}^{-}$\n- ${Z}^{-}$" :question/worked-solution "The positive integer numbers are $1,2,3,…$\n\n- Since all positive integer numbers are natural numbers, all the positive integers belong to $N.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Since all positive integer numbers are positive real numbers, all the positive integer numbers belong to ${R}^{+}.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The set ${Q}^{-}$ contains all the negative rational numbers. However, positive integer numbers as, for instance, $2$ don't belong to ${Q}^{-},$ so ${Q}^{-}$ does *not* contain the positive integer numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set ${Z}^{-}$ contains all the negative integer numbers. However, positive integer numbers as, for instance, $2$ don't belong to ${Z}^{-},$ so ${Z}^{-}$ does *not* contain the positive integer numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f2b31fe-a7f3-55fc-b6eb-7dd3db30f2b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301063} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac71f8c-1c9d-59a7-a383-b29c446451a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301064} {:answer/id #uuid "786916ad-8c4e-5707-b467-f8641b92b687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, III, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301065} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0a820b-3184-5a60-b3fc-cfac7b6d1706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301066} {:answer/id #uuid "68adaa60-2d95-564a-9cb2-30bce7f8a9e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "786916ad-8c4e-5707-b467-f8641b92b687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, III, and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301065} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f7447f1-dd58-576e-916c-ee4188bcee11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3eb6629-ebbb-5e67-b0a8-ec3368f9f0d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-37313" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $\\frac{72}{9}$ belong?\n\n- $N$\n- ${Q}_{0}^{-}$\n- ${Q}^{+}$\n- $R$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that $\\frac{72}{9}=8$ is a natural number, so it belongs to $N.$ \n\nConsequently, $\\frac{72}{9}$ also belongs to ${Q}^{+}$ and $R.$\n\nSince $\\frac{72}{9}$ is positive, it does not belong to ${Q}_{0}^{-}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abc6b3ee-0251-5c9c-9358-bd192c434dd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to Scripted Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02da888f-d748-5049-bb5d-6e8192288fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301070} {:answer/id #uuid "2879d241-6288-52d7-a91f-3939fdd7a443" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301071} {:answer/id #uuid "037d2bd3-59ae-5db1-8228-dfabb40275e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301072} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f57541-b8c8-50ec-81a7-de8c4c419790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301073} {:answer/id #uuid "b04a2888-a83f-5a1c-9f7f-dcdd4acffda4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02da888f-d748-5049-bb5d-6e8192288fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301070} :answer-field/id #uuid "36e033fa-af46-5b3a-886e-d6cc21a8f346" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82428d87-8edc-52b4-a66b-258cbde660a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-37383" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${Q}_{0}^{+}?$\n\n- $0$\n- $\\sqrt{27}$\n- $-\\sqrt{4}$\n- $\\frac{1}{9}$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${Q}_{0}^{+}$ is the set of all positive rational numbers and $0.$\n\n- $0$ belongs to ${Q}_{0}^{+}.\\,✓$\n\n- $\\sqrt{27}=3\\sqrt{3}$ is not a rational number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}_{0}^{+}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\sqrt{4}=-2$ is a negative number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}_{0}^{+}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $\\frac{1}{9}$ is a rational number because it is the ratio of two integers, and moreover, it is a positive rational number. Therefore, $\\frac{1}{9}$ belongs to ${Q}_{0}^{+}.\\,✓$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and IV only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3de9e532-559c-5fc1-a6ad-5fcd1ed77824" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b75be64-ac14-57cf-beef-32c5e70997db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N,Z,Q,R,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301076} {:answer/id #uuid "ef3729a8-9bbf-5561-b4aa-f9824a740a35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301077} {:answer/id #uuid "a2430f8a-4b28-5440-b0a7-1986075339f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301078} {:answer/id #uuid "eac7a46a-da56-5d6f-94e4-aa242a5c5602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301079} {:answer/id #uuid "b956683a-c40d-5bdd-8395-796ab55de33f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef3729a8-9bbf-5561-b4aa-f9824a740a35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301077} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2a8d37e-b421-5b5d-83d8-9562120ff7ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb3a08e1-046c-5655-8701-2c4bac14eb96" :question/math-academy-id "q-80234" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $-5$ belong?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $-5$ is negative, so it does *not* belong to $N,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\notin N.\n$$\n\n- However, $-5$ is an integer, so it does belong to $Z,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Every integer is a rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, $-5$ belongs to $Q,R,$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-5\\in Q,\\,-5\\in R,\\,-5\\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Z,Q,R,$ and $C.$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301081 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "abc6b3ee-0251-5c9c-9358-bd192c434dd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to Scripted Special Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c930386a-5136-50f9-bf20-479eba8d6892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301083} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a66c1e-b543-54e9-ad40-3e1a17d51057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301084} {:answer/id #uuid "08d85b01-5aec-5012-a7ac-13b39491c69d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301085} {:answer/id #uuid "d06a73e0-fd44-541b-9c6e-d6e5a928888b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301086} {:answer/id #uuid "75789265-9f31-5dde-aa0a-9bd5faad30f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75789265-9f31-5dde-aa0a-9bd5faad30f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301087} :answer-field/id #uuid "03c4fb85-a321-5467-af16-32cb80b70300" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6eb8b25b-17d1-576f-87ae-4aad3e36edbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-80300" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${R}_{0}^{+}?$\n\n- $0$\n- $\\sqrt{18}$\n- $-2\\sqrt{5}$\n- $-\\frac{1}{5}$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${R}_{0}^{+}$ is the set of all positive real numbers and $0.$\n\n- $0$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{+}.\\,✓$\n\n- $\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}$ belongs to ${R}_{0}^{+}.\\,✓$\n\n- $-2\\sqrt{5}$ is a negative number, so it does *not* belong to ${R}_{0}^{+}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\frac{1}{5}$ is a negative number, so it does *not* belong to ${R}_{0}^{+}.\\,\\times $\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3de9e532-559c-5fc1-a6ad-5fcd1ed77824" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5486692f-1eb0-5037-a645-b1d4cfabe7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$N,Z,Q,R,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301090} {:answer/id #uuid "23f4b43e-edda-585a-bbc1-30b738dbd4cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301091} {:answer/id #uuid "61c53909-30e8-5e50-8721-b319debc56d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301092} {:answer/id #uuid "87b83bef-3ae9-59af-9500-d2d18f9613b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301093} {:answer/id #uuid "0992376b-0904-55ef-8228-f99f313acf35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23f4b43e-edda-585a-bbc1-30b738dbd4cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301091} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa147b5-3102-5493-aadb-58120a190f2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b502dfb2-0f40-5bef-86cd-aca89e52845b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80331" :question/problem "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nN,\\,Z,\\,Q,\\,R,\\,C\n$$\n\nTo which of these sets does the number $-\\frac{27}{3}$ belong?" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035971/assets/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $-\\frac{27}{3}=-9$ is negative, so it does *not* belong to $N,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\notin N.\n$$\n\n- However, $-9$ is an integer, so it does belong to $Z,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Every integer is a rational, real, and complex number. Consequently, $-\\frac{27}{3}$ belongs to $Q,R,$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n-\\frac{27}{3}\\in Q,\\,-\\frac{27}{3}\\in R,\\,-\\frac{27}{3}\\in C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3de9e532-559c-5fc1-a6ad-5fcd1ed77824" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Special Sets Containing a Given Element"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef93981f-ca33-5734-8cc4-2f2b6b93d8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z,Q,R,$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301097} {:answer/id #uuid "fcbebb9d-33f7-5f0e-b4b1-44af332735ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q,R,$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301098} {:answer/id #uuid "5d894b4e-aa3e-5c6e-a604-5855361246ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Z$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301099} {:answer/id #uuid "b414c357-79d1-5212-a4a0-2482572a0fd5" :answer/type 